{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,90p' phases/49-joint-review-defects/index.json 2>/dev/null || true\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"project\": \"Kijun\",\n  \"phase\": \"49-joint-review-defects\",\n  \"status\": \"completed\",\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"step\": 0,\n      \"name\": \"refute-defect-claims\",\n      \"kind\": \"verify\",\n      \"gate\": true,\n      \"status\": \"completed\",\n      \"summary\": \"C1-C6 hold, each by a mutation or a runnable reproduction. C7 was first recorded as refuted; that refutation was overturned by an independent cross-verification (a modifier-held left drag pans in OrbitControls, so the mechanism is reachable) and is withdrawn — the guard was added and mut6-uc25.js demonstrates it firing. C1's 最上層柱 example and C5's judgment method were also wrong as written and are corrected against the claims.\",\n      \"authored_by\": \"Claude Opus 5 (direct, outside the codex harness — user instruction)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"step\": 1,\n      \"name\": \"joint-target-kind\",\n      \"status\": \"completed\",\n      \"summary\": \"The add button is disabled with the domain's own reason, and openDraft refuses, whenever resolveJoint reports the target unsupported — in ReviewPane and, after cross-verification, in WorkPackageBoard too. openDraft also now takes the finding's own column rather than the ambient selection. No member-kind branch was added to either component.\",\n      \"authored_by\": \"Claude Opus 5 (direct, outside the codex harness — user instruction)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"step\": 2,\n      \"name\": \"stale-notice-coverage\",\n      \"status\": \"completed\",\n      \"summary\": \"The stale replay notice is pinned in both directions from the locale key; inverting its condition fails the test.\",\n      \"authored_by\": \"Claude Opus 5 (direct, outside the codex harness — user instruction)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"step\": 3,\n      \"name\": \"work-package-link-and-assertions\",\n      \"status\": \"completed\",\n      \"summary\": \"The checklist link is now made through the select and read back from the store; the readiness assertion states its own expected value and matches /^準備完了$/ exactly.\",\n      \"authored_by\": \"Claude Opus 5 (direct, outside the codex harness — user instruction)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"step\": 4,\n      \"name\": \"uc25-self-assertion\",\n      \"status\": \"completed\",\n      \"summary\": \"jointCanvas and findingFocus now carry their own observations, a twentieth check fails on any page or console error accumulated across all four page sessions (the first was unwatched until cross-verification), the accumulator drains on read so one error is not counted twice, and schemaVersion must be present on both sides. The C7 camera guard is in: the fingerprint must resolve to at least one rebar on both sides of the drag, and the change must be in a point that reads a rebar.\",\n      \"authored_by\": \"Claude Opus 5 (direct, outside the codex harness — user instruction)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"step\": 5,\n      \"name\": \"cross-verification\",\n      \"kind\": \"verify\",\n      \"status\": \"refuted\",\n      \"summary\": \"Four Antigravity CLI agents, read-only, each on a different scope. Refutations that landed: (a) step 0's refutation of C7 — a modifier-held left drag pans in OrbitControls, so the mechanism IS reachable; (b) WorkPackageBoard has the same unguarded joint target ReviewPane had; (c) openDraft let the ambient selection override the finding's own column; (d) the new diagnostics check misses the first page session, drains before clearStore, never clears the in-page accumulator, and catches almost nothing of value. Surviving: claims A-E on the phase diff, and the C7 guard itself once written. Verdicts kept verbatim as cross-verification-1..4; the index is cross-verification.md.\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"Antigravity CLI (agy, bypermissions), four agents in 